<title>ITALY: Italy's Naples sees Feb CPI at -0.2 pct mo/mo.</title>
<headline>Italy's Naples sees Feb CPI at -0.2 pct mo/mo.</headline>
<dateline>NAPLES, Italy 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Naples said its February consumer price index stood at -0.2 percent month on month and 2.6 percent year on year.</p>
<p>In January, Naples' inflation rate was 0.4 percent and 3.1 percent respectively.</p>
<p>Naples is one of 11 Italian cities to have published inflation data Thursday and Friday.</p>
<p>The city's CPI has a weighting of 6.64 percent on the national index. The 11 sample cities have a combined weighting of 75.66 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes:</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to January 1997)</p>
<p>					  Month/Month	Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		  -0.2 (0.4)	 +2.6  (3.1)</p>
<p>    Food				0.0 (0.2)	 +3.3  (3.8)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	+0.1 (0.0)	 +2.1  (2.1)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges -3.6 (1.4)	-1.2  (2.4)</p>
<p>    Furniture			 0.0 (0.0)	 +1.6  (1.6)</p>
<p>    Health services		+0.2 (2.8)	 +2.6  (2.4)</p>
<p>    Transportation		 +1.0 (0.3)	 +4.8  (5.1)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture  +0.3 (0.0)	 +4.0  (4.3)</p>
<p>    Education			+0.7 (0.0)	 +4.0  (3.4)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants     +0.6 (0.0)	 +3.6  (3.3)</p>
<p>    Other goods and services    0.0 (0.0)	 +1.8  (1.9)</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129589</p>
</text>
